«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses˜„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ&And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¨Make thee two trumpets of silver; of a whole piece shalt thou make them: that thou mayest use them for the calling of the assembly, and for the journeying of the camps.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‰And when they shall blow with them, all the assembly shall assemble themselves to thee at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡And if they blow but with one trumpet, then the princes, which are heads of the thousands of Israel, shall gather themselves unto thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRWhen ye blow an alarm, then the camps that lie on the east parts shall go forward.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—When ye blow an alarm the second time, then the camps that lie on the south side shall take their journey: they shall blow an alarm for their journeys.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙeBut when the congregation is to be gathered together, ye shall blow, but ye shall not sound an alarm.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘And the sons of Aaron, the priests, shall blow with the trumpets; and they shall be to you for an ordinance for ever throughout your generations.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter
