«first_verseªlast_verse¦versesŸ„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜In the first place went the standard of the camp of the children of Judah according to their armies: and over his host was Nahshon the son of Amminadab.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYAnd over the host of the tribe of the children of Issachar was Nethaneel the son of Zuar.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUAnd over the host of the tribe of the children of Zebulun was Eliab the son of Helon.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvAnd the tabernacle was taken down; and the sons of Gershon and the sons of Merari set forward, bearing the tabernacle.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~And the standard of the camp of Reuben set forward according to their armies: and over his host was Elizur the son of Shedeur.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^And over the host of the tribe of the children of Simeon was Shelumiel the son of Zurishaddai.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTAnd over the host of the tribe of the children of Gad was Eliasaph the son of Deuel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqAnd the Kohathites set forward, bearing the sanctuary: and the other did set up the tabernacle against they came.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘And the standard of the camp of the children of Ephraim set forward according to their armies: and over his host was Elishama the son of Ammihud.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\And over the host of the tribe of the children of Manasseh was Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYAnd over the host of the tribe of the children of Benjamin was Abidan the son of Gideoni.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¶And the standard of the camp of the children of Dan set forward, which was the rereward of all the camps throughout their hosts: and over his host was Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTAnd over the host of the tribe of the children of Asher was Pagiel the son of Ocran.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUAnd over the host of the tribe of the children of Naphtali was Ahira the son of Enan.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙeThus were the journeyings of the children of Israel according to their armies, when they set forward.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter
«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙüAnd Moses said unto Hobab, the son of Raguel the Midianite, Moses' father in law, We are journeying unto the place of which the LORD said, I will give it you: come thou with us, and we will do thee good: for the LORD hath spoken good concerning Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[And he said unto him, I will not go; but I will depart to mine own land, and to my kindred.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“And he said, Leave us not, I pray thee; forasmuch as thou knowest how we are to encamp in the wilderness, and thou mayest be to us instead of eyes.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒAnd it shall be, if thou go with us, yea, it shall be, that what goodness the LORD shall do unto us, the same will we do unto thee.¦layout ªlast_verse …¤book§chapter
«first_verse!ªlast_verse$¦verses”„¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¾And they departed from the mount of the LORD three days' journey: and the ark of the covenant of the LORD went before them in the three days' journey, to search out a resting place for them.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙOAnd the cloud of the LORD was upon them by day, when they went out of the camp.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ And it came to pass, when the ark set forward, that Moses said, Rise up, LORD, and let thine enemies be scattered; and let them that hate thee flee before thee.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙOAnd when it rested, he said, Return, O LORD, unto the many thousands of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse$